.TH GLYPTICA 1 "2026" "Livyatan Design Suite" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glyptica \- artwork to cut linework and carved relief
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glyptica
[\fIART.png\fR|\fI.jpg\fR|\fI.svg\fR|\fI.dxf\fR]
.br
.B glyptica rectify
\fIIN OUT\fR \fB\-\-quad\fR \fIx1,y1,...,x4,y4\fR [\fB\-\-size\fR \fIWxH\fR] [\fB\-\-vstretch\fR \fIS\fR]
.br
.B glyptica adjust
\fIIN OUT\fR [\fB\-\-gamma\fR \fIG\fR] [\fB\-\-levels\fR \fIlo,hi\fR]
.br
.B glyptica extract
\fIIN.png OUT-mask.png\fR [\fB\-\-min\-area\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-invert\fR] [\fB\-\-crop\fR \fIx,y,w,h\fR]
.br
.B glyptica refine
\fIIN OUT\fR [\fB\-\-dilate\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-erode\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-close\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-area\fR \fIN\fR]
.br
.B glyptica trace
\fIMASK.png OUT.svg\fR [\fB\-\-speckle\fR \fIN\fR]
.br
.B glyptica place
\fIMASK PREVIEW.png\fR [\fB\-\-offset\fR \fIdx,dy\fR] [\fB\-\-scale\fR \fIsx,sy\fR] [\fB\-\-shear\fR \fIs\fR]
.br
.B glyptica emboss
\fIMASK OUT.stl\fR [\fB\-\-mm\fR \fIH\fR] [\fB\-\-thick\fR \fIT\fR] [\fB\-\-depth\fR \fID\fR] [\fB\-\-raise\fR] [\fB\-\-offset\fR \fIdx,dy\fR] [\fB\-\-scale\fR \fIsx,sy\fR] [\fB\-\-shear\fR \fIs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Glyphs into matter. rectify un-warps a hand-held photo (read the page
corners off any viewer); extract pulls a clean stroke mask through an
adaptive threshold; trace vectorizes it for a laser; emboss carves it into
a relief slab in the art's own shape. Bare invocation opens the window, which runs the whole chain: open a
photograph, flatten it by clicking four page corners, threshold, clean,
place, then export SVG linework or a relief slab STL.
adjust lifts a dim photo (gamma, black/white levels) before extract;
refine grows, thins, or closes strokes; place renders a PNG preview of the
placement flags emboss will use.
emboss cuts the strokes in (intaglio) unless \-\-raise, which stands them
proud (emboss). Output is one closed solid: print it, or boolean it onto a part in
structor.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gilgamesh (1),
.BR hephaestus (1),
.BR livyatan (7).
